  "notes": "Current NMU bulletin Biology Major with General Biology concentration. Total 120 = biology core 24 + concentration electives 20 + other required 19 + gen-ed 33 + free electives 24 (no minor required). Concentration electives: any BI 200+ with at least 12 cr at 300+ (not BI 305); chosen: BI 303 General Microbiology (5), BI 327 Animal Physiology (4), BI 322 Vertebrate Zoology (4), BI 230 Plant Kingdom (4), BI 423 Parasitology (3) = 20 cr with 16 cr at 300 level. Organic chemistry via CH 315 + CH 317 (4 cr). BI/CH/PH courses carry SCII; MA 161 carries QUAR. Free electives are student-choice slots. BI 489 (0 cr) is a required zero-credit assessment. Semester placement is a constructed sample sequence following course-number order.",
